Kind: ablation
Issue: #787
Over: 787-widen-doassign-window.patch
Takes out: thread_doassign()'s check, after the retry, that the thread is not already in the set it is being moved to (#787 section 4) -- the retry substitutes the default set for the one destroyed, and for a default-set thread that makes the two the same, so the lock loop locks the default set's mutex a second time and sleeps holding it. doassign_test's assignment does not come back.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 66 300 -smp 4
Expect: doassign_test: WRONG .* did not come back

